 "verdict": "Measured sink strength and read stored phi on 6 model(s); 6 have both the raw and bos arms needed for the PRIMARY. PRIMARY, BOS: Falcon3-1B-Base sink(raw3) 0.6826->0.7229 (d +0.0403), phi 0.214->0.906 (d +0.693); Minerva-3B-base-v1.0 sink(raw3) 0.5985->0.6660 (d +0.0675), phi 0.328->0.005 (d -0.323); pythia-410m-deduped sink(raw3) 0.6251->0.6054 (d -0.0197), phi 0.427->0.005 (d -0.422); Qwen1.5-1.8B sink(raw3) 0.7135->0.7433 (d +0.0298), phi 0.510->0.000 (d -0.510); SmolLM-1.7B sink(raw3) 0.6263->0.7748 (d +0.1484), phi 0.562->0.000 (d -0.562); Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct sink(raw3) 0.6638->0.6394 (d -0.0244), phi n/a.  SIGN AGREEMENT, the decisive quantity: sink and phi move the same way on 2 of 5 models (['Falcon3-1B-Base', 'pythia-410m-deduped']). Sink strength does NOT predict the sign of the fixed-point shift -- agreement is at or near chance. The attention-sink account, at this context length, does not explain the domain effect's direction, and paper 2's discrepancy stands with both quantities now measured on the same forward passes rather than one of them assumed. Separately, the literature's UNIFORMITY claim does not reproduce here: d(sink) is NOT uniform in sign across the 6 measured models (2 of 6 go DOWN under BOS). That is a statement about THIS context length only -- the sink literature measures long contexts, where the phenomenon is about attention concentrating despite many competing positions. It is not a refutation of that work. SECONDARY (EXPLORATORY, declared before the numbers -- 6 model clusters cannot fail a rank correlation informatively, so no p-value is computed): across 5 (model, arm) cells, d(sink) and d(phi) are Falcon3-1B-Base/bos: +0.0403 vs +0.693; Minerva-3B-base-v1.0/bos: +0.0675 vs -0.323; pythia-410m-deduped/bos: -0.0197 vs -0.422; Qwen1.5-1.8B/bos: +0.0298 vs -0.510; SmolLM-1.7B/bos: +0.1484 vs -0.562. BOUNDARY: sink strength is defined ONCE here -- mean attention from the last position to position 0, over all layers and heads, across 16 random two-token starts, at the census's own context length. The sink literature measures on LONG contexts where streaming matters; a null here bounds that account at this context length and does not refute it in general. phi is read from stored censuses, never recomputed.",
